# Job 18: PHP builds $_SERVER with interned fixed names and a presized array.
# Branch perf/php-server-interned. B is master plus that commit.
# 597 wave 4, src/nxt_php_sapi.c.
# PREREQUISITE: the "server" workload, a PHP script that reads $_SERVER.
# The lab has hello, static1k and capp only. Apply
# jobs/18-runner-server-workload.patch to the harness first (git apply
# from the harness root). It adds the workload to perf-job.sh and cells.sh
# and adds www/server.php. Until then perf-job.sh refuses WORKLOAD=server.
# Callgrind on PHP 8.5.10 with opcache, root target, 3 header fields:
# 52,665 to 49,394 instructions per request inside nxt_php_request_handler,
# -3,272 (-6.2%). The lab's s_instructions also counts libunit and the
# router, so the expected change there is smaller, about 2 to 3 percent, at
# the null band (2.5 to 2.6 percent). Syscalls do not change.
JOB=18-php-server-interned
ISSUE=https://github.com/freeunitorg/freeunit/issues/597
REV_A=origin/master
REV_B=origin/master
PATCH_B=patches/php-server-interned.diff
WORKLOAD=server
CONNS=6
WARM=2
DUR=8
REPS=4
PERF=1
STRACE=1
PRIMARY=s_instructions
FUNCS=php.unit.so:nxt_php_register_variables
EXPECT=s_instructions down about 3,300 per request (near the null band); every asys_ and rsys_ syscall count equal in A and B; nxt_php_register_variables larger in B (inlined registration)
FALSIFY=s_instructions higher in B than the null band, or any syscall count that differs between A and B
